# Remote calibration runs (M3)

## Output layout

Each SLURM job ID gets a folder under `outputs/<job_id>/<iso3>/<analysis_type>/`
with the standard files from `store_outputs` (`updates.h5`, `spaghetti.h5`,
`idata_filtered.nc`, etc.).

## Which copy is used for analysis

`get_analysis_paths(FULL_RUN, countries)` in `emu_renewal.utils` walks
`FULL_RUN` in order and takes the first usable folder for each
country–analysis pair. See `FULL_RUN` in `code/emu_renewal/constants.py`.

Usable means `analysis_output_status(path)` returns `"usable"` (finished
outputs and `idata_filtered.nc` at least `MIN_IDATA_BYTES`).

## Full country run (all analysis types per country)

Runs every analysis type from `get_analyses_for_country` for each country in
`data/config/oxcgrt_included.json`. Mobility types with no scaler CSV are
skipped with a log warning.

```bash
# On M3 login node, from repo root — set array size to number of countries
sbatch --array=1-126 --export=SCRIPT_DIR=$PWD/scripts/massive/jtrauer \
  scripts/massive/jtrauer/run_countries.sh
```

`run_countries.py` takes the job ID (`$SLURM_ARRAY_JOB_ID`) and array task index.

## Targeted rerun (specific country–analysis pairs)

1. Run `notebooks/running/04-identify-reruns.ipynb` locally after syncing
   `outputs/`. This writes `data/config/rerun_pairs.json`.
2. Submit from repo root:

```bash
bash scripts/massive/jtrauer/launch.sh
```

That sizes the array from `rerun_pairs.json` and runs `rerun_countries.py`,
one pair per task.

## After a remote run

Sync new `outputs/<job_id>/` folders locally, prepend the job ID to `FULL_RUN`
if it should take precedence, and re-run `04-identify-reruns.ipynb` to refresh
`rerun_pairs.json`.
